            <ArticleTitle>Sustained benefit of painful legs moving toes syndrome with botulinum toxin type A.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1031-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jocn.2012.06.016</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0967-5868(12)00579-6</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Painful legs moving toes (PLMT) is a rare disorder characterized by an often-severe painful sensation in the legs associated with involuntary movement of the toes. The treatment can be challenging given the poor response to pharmacotherapy. We present a patient with PLMT who obtained substantial benefit in both pain and severity of involuntary movement with botulinum toxin type A injections for more than 3 years.</AbstractText>
